# The packaging's two generated files. debian/changelog is what dpkg reads the
# version from, so whatever writes it is the release process -- here that is
# debian/make-changelog, from CHANGELOG.md and `git describe` (#50 §9). It has
# to exist before dpkg-buildpackage starts, which is why it is generated rather
# than built. The NEWS file's prose is committed as *.NEWS.in; only its version
# stamp comes from the same place the changelog's does.
/changelog
/kerbridge-config.NEWS

# What the build hands the packaging: the six static musl binaries, the fifteen
# generated man pages and THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES, at the paths they install to.
# debian/stage-prebuilt fills it; debian/rules only stages it. Never committed
# -- these are build outputs, and the whole point of generating the man pages is
# that no copy of them is kept.
/prebuilt/
